{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q414924","formula":"FeAl₂(PO₄)₂(OH)₂·6H₂O","hill":"Al2FeH14O16P2","elements":["H","O","Al","P","Fe"],"composition":{"H":14.0,"O":16.0,"P":2.0,"Al":2.0,"Fe":1.0},"names":{"en":"Vauxite","ru":"Воксит","uk":"Воксит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Vauxite is a phosphate mineral with the chemical formula Fe2+Al2(PO4)2(OH)2·6(H2O). It belongs to the laueite – paravauxite group, paravauxite subgroup, although Mindat puts it as a member of the vantasselite Al4(PO4)3(OH)3·9H2O group. There is no similarity in structure between vauxite and paravauxite Fe2+Al2(PO4)2(OH)2·8H2O or metavauxite Fe3+Al2(PO4)2(OH)2·8H2O, even though they are closely similar chemically and all minerals occur together as secondary minerals.","ru":"Воксит — редкий вторичный минерал из класса фосфатов, открыт в 1922 году в Боливии в оловорудном месторождении Льяльягуа. По составу близок к паравокситу и метавокситу, отличаясь от них меньшим количеством молекул воды. Растворим в соляной кислоте.","uk":"Воксит (рос. воксит; англ. vauxite; нім."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q414924","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vauxite-27142.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q4008652","formu